  {
    "sha": "d03e58e2da41df98332ccc516cd8a7d446acb2ae",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGQwM2U1OGUyZGE0MWRmOTgzMzJjY2M1MTZjZDhhN2Q0NDZhY2IyYWU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T13:50:53Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-12T13:50:53Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): EDM conditions bound the wire from below and the gap on its own\n\nReview of 65588c59, blockers 1 and 2. condition_refusal accepted a wire\nof any small diameter and a gap of any size when the condition stated no\nwire beside it:\n\n- wire_diameter is now in [MIN_WIRE_MM, MAX_WIRE_MM] = [0.02, 1] mm, the\n  low end of the same cited range. A mm file's 0.010 (an inch value in\n  the wrong unit) refuses by id, key, value and unit; an inch file's\n  0.010 in (0.254 mm) still passes.\n- gap is bounded on its own, (0, MAX_GAP_MM] = (0, 0.5] mm (half the\n  largest wire), so a 5 mm gap refuses with or without a wire.\n- On a sinker, gap > undersize refuses when both are stated: an\n  electrode undersized less than its spark gap burns past the finished\n  wall. Equal values pass.\n\nPinned in the_kerf_geometry_is_bounded_by_name (mm 0.010 wire, wire C1\ngap 5, sinker E1 gap 5 / undersize 0.1, sinker E1 gap 0.3 / undersize\n0.1, plus the edges that must pass) and in\na_hand_edited_project_machine_with_a_bad_table_is_not_sane (the sinker\nrule at the project gate). assets/machines/AGENTS.md's key table states\nthe new bounds.\n\nRefs #531\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
